## Data Dictionary

# About Dataset
This is an Superstore Customer Sales dataset, it contains:

No. of columns: 20
No. of Records: 8511

# Columns Overview:

## Row ID
An identification number for every row in the table.

## Order ID
An identification number for every transaction made by a customer.

## Order Date
Tracks the date on which the transaction was made (e.g. 2023-05-19).

## Ship Mode
Tracks the class in which the order was shipped. (e.g. Standard Class, Second Class).

## Customer ID
Tracks the customer's ID.

## Customer Name
Tracks the customer's name.

## Segment
Tracks the type of customer making the purchase (e.g. Corporate, Consumer).

## Country/Region
Tracks the country of the customer (e.g. United States).

## City
Tracks the city of the customer (e.g. New York City, Mesa).

## State
Tracks the state the customer lives in (e.g. California, Texas).

## Postal Code
Tracks the postal code of the customers area (e.g. 10024).

## Region
Tracks the geographic region of the customer (e.g. South, West).

## Product ID
Tracks the id of the product.

## Category
Tracks the category of every product ordered (e.g. Office Supplies). 

## Sub-Category
Tracks the sub category of every product ordered (e.g. Paper). 

## Product Name
Tracks the name of the product (e.g. Headphones, Dress).

## Sales
Tracks the final amount after the discount is applied.

## Quantity
Tracks the number of products purchased in every transaction.

## Discount
Tracks the discount applied (e.g. 0.7, 0.2).

## Profit
Tracks the profit made on every transaction.


